#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Read a mini4pro on-phone flight log, and diagnose why the aircraft moved wrong.

Reads the `mini4pro-flightlog-1` JSONL the phone writes and answers two questions. **What
happened** — `--summary`, the default: duration, entry counts, dropped entries *and when*, the
mode timeline, virtual-stick engagement, events. **Why did it move the wrong way** —
`--diagnose-axis`: a time-aligned table of commanded axis, value and control mode against the
resulting NED velocity, attitude and altitude rate, then a conclusion in plain words naming
which of the eight cases the evidence supports, or a statement that the data is insufficient
and what is missing.

    tools/flightlog session.001.jsonl                       # summary
    tools/flightlog 20260801-*.jsonl                        # all parts of a session
    tools/flightlog session.001.jsonl --diagnose-axis       # auto-pick the window
    tools/flightlog s.jsonl --diagnose-axis --around 83.4 --window 3
    tools/flightlog s.jsonl --diagnose-axis --from 80 --to 90
    tools/flightlog s.jsonl --cross-check flight.tlog       # against QGC's own record
    tools/flightlog --list-cases                            # the eight cases
    tools/flightlog --selftest                              # planted faults, all caught

Exits non-zero if a diagnosis is inconclusive (so it can gate a test session) and if any
self-test profile is missed.

Full rationale — the record's format, how to read each mode's output, and the self-test's
seventeen planted faults: `docs/flight-recording.md`.
"""

import argparse
import bisect
import glob
import itertools
import json
import math
import os
import re
